From 7c91758acb114acc95a51cbd9ae96dcdd68b86ae Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Andrey Borodin <amborodin@acm.org>
Date: Mon, 3 Aug 2026 23:59:15 +0500
Subject: [PATCH v1] Document a CHECK_FOR_INTERRUPTS call with interrupts held

CHECK_FOR_INTERRUPTS() cannot process pending interrupts while an LWLock is
held.  The stats-file writer calls it while dshash sequential iteration holds
the current hash partition lock, but that constraint is not apparent at the
call itself.

Mark the call with a grep-friendly comment and describe the lock responsible.
This changes no behavior.

Discussion: https://postgr.es/m/CAA3qoJkBf6H7KukXTWFWCYnf_GHf354kOdWATCfoK%3D-bgdwTJw%40mail.gmail.com
---
 src/backend/utils/activity/pgstat.c | 4 ++++
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/backend/utils/activity/pgstat.c b/src/backend/utils/activity/pgstat.c
index 50cd07822b4..916089a3c2f 100644
--- a/src/backend/utils/activity/pgstat.c
+++ b/src/backend/utils/activity/pgstat.c
@@ -1729,6 +1729,10 @@ pgstat_write_statsfile(void)
 		PgStatShared_Common *shstats;
 		const PgStat_KindInfo *kind_info = NULL;
 
+		/*
+		 * CHECK_FOR_INTERRUPTS_WITH_INTERRUPTS_HELD: dshash_seq_next()
+		 * returns with the current hash partition lock still held.
+		 */
 		CHECK_FOR_INTERRUPTS();
 
 		/*
